  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33543,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 1819,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p><strong>Table&nbsp;3.01</strong> Histological features of fibroadenoma and benign, borderline, and malignant phyllodes tumours</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "<p>Adapted from Lakhani SR, Ellis IO, Schnitt SJ, Tan PH, van de Vijver MJ (Eds): WHO Classification of Tumours of the Breast. IARC: Lyon 2012.</p>",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"width: 446.3pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Histological feature</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Fibroadenoma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 267.8pt; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-left: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; border-right: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"367\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"text-align: center;\" align=\"center\"><strong>Phyllodes tumours</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Benign</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Borderline</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Malignant<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Tumour border</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Well defined</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Well defined</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Well defined, may be focally permeative</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Permeative</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Stromal cellularity</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Variable, scant to uncommonly cellular, usually uniform</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cellular, usually mild, may be non-uniform or diffuse</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cellular, usually moderate, may be non-uniform or diffuse</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cellular, usually marked and diffuse</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Stromal atypia</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">None</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mild or none</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Mild or moderate</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Marked</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mitotic activity</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Usually none, rarely low</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Usually low: &lt;&nbsp;2.5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (&lt;&nbsp;5&nbsp;per 10&nbsp;HPFs)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Usually frequent: 2.5 to &lt; 5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (5&ndash;9 per 10&nbsp;HPFs)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Usually abundant: &ge;&nbsp;5&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup> (&ge;&nbsp;10&nbsp;per 10&nbsp;HPFs)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Stromal overgrowth</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent (or very focal)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Often present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Malignant heterologous elements</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Absent</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">May be present</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Distribution relative to all breast tumours</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Common</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Uncommon</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rare</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"111\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Relative proportion of all phyllodes tumours</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"117\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">n/a</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"132\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">60&ndash;75%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.25pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"114\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">15&ndash;26%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 89.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"120\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">8&ndash;20%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33570,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 6852,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Malignant Phyllodes tumor",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Malignant Phyllodes tumor shows sheets of epithelioid and plump spindled cells with moderately-to-markedly pleomorphic nuclei and brisk mitoses. Necrotic zones and permeative margins are present. Focally, benign epithelium is observed capping detached frond-like portions of the tumor. ",
    "source": "Puay Hoon Tan",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/6852.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33622,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 7655,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Malignant Phylodes Tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Malignant phyllodes tumour shows sheets of epithelioid and plump spindled cells with moderate to markedly pleomorphic nuclei and brisk mitoses.&nbsp; Necrotic zones and permeative margins are present.&nbsp; Focally, benign epithelium is observed capping detached frond-like portions of the tumour.</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/7655.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33623,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 7656,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Malignant Phyllodes tumour with osteosarcoma, chrondrosarcoma and rhabdomyosarcoma.</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Malignant phyllodes tumour shows stromal overgrowth, necrosis and malignant heterologous elements comprising osteosarcoma, chrondrosarcoma and rhabdomyosarcoma.</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/7656.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33624,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 7657,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Bordeline Phyllodes tumour</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Borderline phyllodes tumour shows a partly permeative border with stromal cells displaying moderate cytologic atypia.</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/7657.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33625,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 7658,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Benign phyllodes Tumour with stromal giant cell</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Phyllodes tumour shows broad fronds projecting into cystic spaces.&nbsp; Multinucleated stromal giant cells are seen, and while these can be observed in benign phyllodes tumours without impacting grade assessment, the presence of atypia in other stromal cells as well as the finding of increased mitoses in this case warrants consideration of a borderline grade.</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/7658.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33626,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 7659,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Benign phyllodes tumours with squamoid nests</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Benign phyllodes tumour shows elongated epithelium-lined clefts with areas of mild stromal hypercellularity.&nbsp; The borders of circumscribed and pushing, without any stromal overgrowth, significant stromal atypia or mitotic activity.&nbsp; Focally, sclerotic portions of the stroma show small epithelial nests that have a squamoid appearance.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/7659.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 33627,
    "bookid": 32,
    "chapterId": 52,
    "fileId": 7660,
    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Malignant phyllodes tumours with liposarcoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Malignant phyllodes tumour shows broad stromal fronds, hypercellularity, moderate to marked atypia and mitotic activity. Adipocytes are present within the tumour, which in areas display hyperchromatic scalloped nuclei in keeping with lipoblasts of liposarcoma. Presence of liposarcoma alone is not currently regarded as being diagnostic of a malignant grade in phyllodes tumour. In this case, malignancy is concluded based on a constellation of histological parameters.</p>",
